  "description": "Yapchick (alternatively spelled Yaptzik) is a popular Jewish Passover dish of unknown origin. It's delicious at any time of year and often served on Shabbat! The slow-baked overnight potato kugel is improved only by the delicious meat hiding on the bottom.",
